#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229610 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05af3055-c035-5e11-8946-8791c21a18ac" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Function on Which to Apply a Root-Finding Method When Applying the Trapezoidal Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f195b54-0ce6-5a05-8e50-a1f62e3633f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371155} {:answer/id #uuid "160e84c4-5c45-5dbf-804a-cb8c45fce94a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371156} {:answer/id #uuid "85bfffa6-4043-5c92-99fe-048ea46b0822" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371157} {:answer/id #uuid "275ba559-a2c3-5f6f-95c9-a7bc4ad724ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371158} {:answer/id #uuid "492b96bf-4215-53a6-adfc-742d1fe9e8b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "160e84c4-5c45-5dbf-804a-cb8c45fce94a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371156} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5cc6747-a74a-5506-9d19-89bac4895967" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35c595ff-be2a-5f4a-860e-75bace791ff8" :question/math-academy-id "q-333428" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x{y}^{2},\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2x{y}^{2}+2{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =x{y}^{2}+{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+x{y}^{2}+{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-y-x{y}^{2}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-y-x{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-2({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-1-1(1)^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-2({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05af3055-c035-5e11-8946-8791c21a18ac" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Function on Which to Apply a Root-Finding Method When Applying the Trapezoidal Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c4123e1-be0c-5705-b860-30cb58e63d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-{x}_{\\text{new}}\\sqrt{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371162} {:answer/id #uuid "bd6a96b0-69e1-5319-8d67-72cddc7da278" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-x\\sqrt{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371163} {:answer/id #uuid "2ac52f16-54bd-505d-8449-3f902f9e0f00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-x\\sqrt{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371164} {:answer/id #uuid "f94ae7de-b59c-5650-bc70-521b91251c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2{x}_{\\text{new}}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-2x\\sqrt{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371165} {:answer/id #uuid "dd24646b-6011-5ee5-8fd9-550fa0ace3ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}+{x}_{\\text{new}}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-x\\sqrt{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd6a96b0-69e1-5319-8d67-72cddc7da278" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-x\\sqrt{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371163} :answer-field/id #uuid "39ab2fe3-fb33-5cae-9585-f54d210f73a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f0aeadd-83c8-5927-a330-f514da963230" :question/math-academy-id "q-334061" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x\\sqrt{y},\\,y(0)=3\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current values $x$ and $y?$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2x\\sqrt{y}+2{x}_{\\text{new}}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =x\\sqrt{y}+{x}_{\\text{new}}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+x\\sqrt{y}+{x}_{\\text{new}}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n{{{y}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-x\\sqrt{y}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-y-x\\sqrt{y}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "05af3055-c035-5e11-8946-8791c21a18ac" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Function on Which to Apply a Root-Finding Method When Applying the Trapezoidal Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be439f3d-147b-592b-abf9-eff4b20f808f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371169} {:answer/id #uuid "275713b7-2edf-5614-ac61-6a8ff5eef957" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}+\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371170} {:answer/id #uuid "45f16e9a-dd5e-5661-a0bf-22ed4161d129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}+\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371171} {:answer/id #uuid "615d2361-2aa8-543d-b01f-c4d8e0d759ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}+2\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371172} {:answer/id #uuid "b7dc6508-8de0-5bc0-bd7a-7f178cef544f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}+\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45f16e9a-dd5e-5661-a0bf-22ed4161d129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}+\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371171} :answer-field/id #uuid "afd17de6-459c-5f97-8e0f-d03fb36548b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f4261307-0c79-5182-bcee-cbb66ec60810" :question/math-academy-id "q-334151" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x-2\\sqrt{y},\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-2\\sqrt{y}+{x}_{\\text{new}}-2\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}-\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}-\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMoving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}+\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}}+\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\n Therefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-1-\\frac{1}{2}(1)-\\frac{1}{2}(2)+1+\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-1-\\frac{1}{2}-1+1+\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}+\\sqrt{{y}_{\\text{new}}}-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e885f33-5bef-5c95-8afa-495b6512e398" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating the Solution to an Initial Value Problem Using the Trapezoidal Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32586168-50d0-5006-91db-e33a7e2d6a60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371176} {:answer/id #uuid "2a2b4d44-2233-5d53-b955-50f98510173f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a2b4d44-2233-5d53-b955-50f98510173f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371177} :answer-field/id #uuid "46f94d6f-a13c-514f-9a65-8a809db285dc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c2dc2b4-b07f-50ff-84ba-476c569db1bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-334450" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x-{y}^{3},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with one step and Newton's method to approximate $y(1).$ Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n$y(1)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((x-{y}^{3})+({x}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0.5x-0.5{y}^{3}+0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5x-0.5{y}^{3}+0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}+0.5{y}^{3}-y-0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.5x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}+0.5{y}^{3}-y-0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.5x.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+1=1.\n$$\n\n Then, the function $g$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}+0.5(1)^{3}-1-0.5\\cdot 1-0.5\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use a root-finding method with starting point $y=1$ to solve $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.$ We'll use Newton's method:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}{{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})}.\n$$\n\nNote that the derivative of $g$ is\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})=1.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton's method iterative scheme is as follows:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{0.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{3}+({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-1}{1.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nApplying several iterations of Newton's method starting with $y(0)=1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{\\text{new}})_{1} & =1 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{2} & =0.8 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{3} & ≈0.771\\,429 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{4} & ≈0.770\\,917\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈0.77,$ rounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e885f33-5bef-5c95-8afa-495b6512e398" :knowledge-point/title "Approximating the Solution to an Initial Value Problem Using the Trapezoidal Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e3b1c6a-5f10-5a0b-b554-702c042a9547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e3b1c6a-5f10-5a0b-b554-702c042a9547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371180} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4a61420-9628-5a12-9eee-f7713d448e99" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44a5a027-2564-5020-9ef7-18a590f676a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-334470" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=1-x{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse the trapezoidal method with one step and Newton's method to approximate $y(1).$ Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n$y(1)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((1-x{y}^{2})+(1-{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1-0.5x{y}^{2}-0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+1-0.5x{y}^{2}-0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-1+0.5x{y}^{2}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-1+0.5x{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+1=1.\n$$\n\nThen, the function $g$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5(1)({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-1-1+0.5(0)(1)^{2} \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use a root-finding method with starting point $y=1$ to solve $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.$ We'll use Newton's method:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}{{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})}.\n$$\n\nNote that the derivative of $g$ is\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})=({y}_{\\text{new}})+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton's method iterative scheme is as follows:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{0.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{2}+({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-2}{({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}+1}.\n$$\n\nApplying several iterations of Newton's method starting with $y(0)=1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{\\text{new}})_{1} & =1 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{2} & =1.25 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{3} & ≈1.236\\,111 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{4} & ≈1.236\\,068\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈1.24,$ rounded to two decimal places."}]}
